  "query_preview": "..\nAn area of surface convergence embedded within the monsoon trough and\na trailing surface trough from the north will bring wetter weather \nover the Marianas, particularly over Guam and Rota. Scattered \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms are expected this evening, \nincreasing to numerous showers for Guam and Rota after midnight and \ncontinuing through Wednesday night. Locally heavy showers are \npossible during this time period, although, flash flood concerns are \ntoo low for any hydrology products at this time. So, opted for a \nheadline for Guam and Rota to indicate the possibility for locally \nheavy rainfall and stronger gusts within those showers. Then, the \nmonsoon trough will remain active near Guam and Rota through the rest\nof the week, whereas Saipan and Tinian will see a reduction in winds\nand shower coverage shortly after midweek. Looking towards the end \nof the week, models indicate a tropical disturbance potentially \nforming over the region or to the west. Due to disagreements between \nmodel solutions and a lack of any notable circulations on satellite, \nuncertainty is high regarding this pattern, so the weekend forecast \ntops out at 30 and 40 percent between the two zones. Finally, benign \nconditions are possible next week during the holiday.",
